{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"verdict\": \"discrepancy\",\n  \"statementAssessment\": \"The exposition asserts a single real y that works for every real x. This is false. The formal proposition instead allows y to depend on x.\",\n  \"methodAssessment\": \"No proof method or formal argument is supplied; only the formal proposition is stated. Method correspondence cannot be assessed.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"sourceAssertion\": \"There is a real y such that x+y=0 for every real x.\",\n      \"formalCounterpart\": \"For every real x, there exists real y with x+y=0.\",\n      \"classification\": \"discrepancy: quantifier order changes the claim\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The exposition requires one fixed y for all x; the formal proposition permits a different y for each x. The formal proposition is true, but it does not express the exposition’s assertion.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"If a fixed y works for every x, taking x=0 forces y=0. Taking x=1 then requires 1+0=0, which is false.\",\n      \"uncertainty\": \"None about the quantifier mismatch or the counterexample.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"examinedAssertions\": [\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“There is a real y such that x+y=0 for every real x.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"False as written.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"x=0 forces y=0, but then x=1 does not satisfy x+y=0.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"assertion\": \"“For every real x, there exists real y with x+y=0.”\",\n      \"assessment\": \"True, and not equivalent to the exposition.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"For each x, choosing y=-x gives x+y=0.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"omissions\": [\n    \"No proof or method accompanies the formal proposition, so there is no argument to compare.\"\n  ],\n  \"toolsUsed\": [\n    \"Read /input/INPUT.md with cat.\"\n  ],\n  \"checkingStatus\": \"No Lean checks run; the input contains a rendered proposition, not an original Lean module.\"\n}"}}
